        You will be provided with a patch used to fix a bug. 
        Based on the commit message and modifications in the patch, you need to analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. 

        Here is the patch content:
        From 57038afa171acdc8140016bbb84dacbd13c417bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drew DeVault <sir@cmpwn.com>
Date: Tue, 2 May 2017 20:46:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Do not zero RGB pixels if A == 0 (#43)

This fixes a problem introduced by
5ed200d5d73edc54969b34c708d18728d38c070b.
---
 src/pngcodec.c | 14 +++++---------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/pngcodec.c b/src/pngcodec.c
index bac40b1..c51188d 100644
--- a/src/pngcodec.c
+++ b/src/pngcodec.c
@@ -455,16 +455,12 @@ gdip_load_png_image_from_file_or_stream (FILE *fp, GetBytesDelegate getBytesFunc
 				for (i = 0; i < height; i++) {
 					png_bytep rowp = row_pointers[i];
 					for (j = 0; j < width; j++) {
+						BYTE b = rowp[2];
+						BYTE g = rowp[1];
+						BYTE r = rowp[0];
 						BYTE a = rowp[3];
-						if (a == 0) {
-							set_pixel_bgra (rawptr, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0);
-						} else {
-							BYTE b = rowp[2];
-							BYTE g = rowp[1];
-							BYTE r = rowp[0];
-
-							set_pixel_bgra (rawptr, 0, b, g, r, a);
-						}
+
+						set_pixel_bgra (rawptr, 0, b, g, r, a);
 						rowp += 4;
 						rawptr += 4;
 					}
-- 
2.25.1



        Provide a response strictly in the following format:
        Root cause:<Root cause>

    You are a programming expert.
    You will be given the root cause of a bug and  the corresponding patch.
    You need to extract the code statements that lead to the bug from  the patch, based on the root cause.


    Provide a response strictly in the following format:
    Code statements:
    <text1>
    <text2>
    <text3>
    <text4>
    ...
    <textN>

Root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect handling of pixels with an alpha value of 0. The original code zeroed out the RGB values when the alpha channel was 0, which is unnecessary and incorrect. Instead, the RGB values should be preserved even when the alpha is 0, allowing for proper transparency handling in the image processing. The patch corrects this by always setting the pixel values using the RGB values from the PNG data, regardless of the alpha value.
